   "updated_at": "2026-11-02T19:10:18Z",
   "body": "Second shape, found by code review round 5 of #444 (ADR 0014 §4, commit 1eb50fa on #442): **deeply nested blocks**. `[quote]`×n or `[spoiler]`×n is a table in a table n deep, and **both** SwiftSoup parses (page parse and normalizer) grow quadratically in the depth, the writer staying linear:\n\n| Nested `[quote]…[/quote]` | size | page parse | normalizer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 000 | 15 KB | 3.6 s | 3.8 s |\n| 2 000 | 30 KB | 14 s | 14 s |\n\nDebug build, Linux. Same conclusion as the crossed tags: the output is right, the time is at stake, the reader pays it on a posted message and the preview on a draft. A SwiftSoup parse cannot be cancelled, so LOT-152 skips the live preview above a depth or size it sets (an on-demand preview stays possible). Fixing it here means either a bound in the reader before the parse (depth or size of the HTML) or a cheaper tree builder for nested tables.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
